{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>None of you shall approach any near of kin.</b> Now, the offspring produced from near of kin, when the agent and recipient are close in temperament, should properly be more fitting and well-tempered — as happened with the offspring of Moses, Aaron, and Miriam from Amram and Jochebed his aunt, and as the Sages of blessed memory said regarding marriage to one's niece. This holds true when the agent and recipient intend solely to fulfill the will of their Maker. However, this occurs only rarely; for what happens in the entire human species, or in the majority, is that they intend pleasure alone, as it says: הֵן בְּעָווֹן חוֹלָלְתִּי וּבְחֵטְא יֶחֱמַתְנִי אִמִּי (Psalms 51:7). And since near of kin are exceedingly prone to this, and the imagination and pleasure involved are very great — when both think their union is not forbidden, the imagination and union between them for mere pleasure will multiply; thus they consort without restraint and the land fills with licentiousness. Therefore Scripture says <b>to uncover nakedness</b>, for indeed the pleasure of uncovering alone is what is intended in the majority of cases. Accordingly, the Torah forbade all blood relations and those close to this line at one degree. The degrees of proximity the Torah counts from both the man and the woman equally. Thus it forbade the father's sister, who is at the first degree from the father, and permitted the brother's daughter, who is at the second degree from him. And it forbade the father's wife, the brother's wife, and the uncle's wife, even after their husbands' death, even though they are not blood relations at all — because they are reckoned at the degree of their husbands. And along these lines the prohibition of all forbidden unions appears to be set."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:47.738830351Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}